family: set-cli
what: syslog
transport: udp
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: common set-style syslog statements (set system syslog host …); RFC 5424 severities and facilities
does: Sends the device's log messages, informational and more severe, to Woodshed over UDP.
check: The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard after the commit, with its first message.
placeholders: 
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- `any info` sends every facility at info and above; the facility and level keywords differ slightly between devices.
- `structured-data` asks for RFC 5424 messages where the device offers it; leave the line out if it doesn't.
- Set the address the messages come from with `set system syslog source-address <address>` if the device has several; Woodshed shows that address as the device.
---- part cli "": Enter in configuration mode, then commit
set system syslog host 192.0.2.10 any info
set system syslog host 192.0.2.10 port 514
set system syslog host 192.0.2.10 structured-data
commit
